          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#in_the_wick_algebra_of_free_quantum_fields"} In the Wick algebra of free quantum fields
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            What are called
            %em Weyl relations
            is the incarnation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+commutation+relations"} canonical commutation relations
            under passing to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponentials"} exponentials
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weyl+algebra"} Weyl algebra
          %p
            For example if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi a
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a, a^\ast
            are two elements of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutator"} commutator
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi a
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℏ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [a,a^\ast] = \hbar
          %p
            then the corresponding Weyl relation is, by the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Baker-Campbell-Hausdorff+formula"} Baker-Campbell-Hausdorff formula
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %mi z
                      %mi a
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi z
                        %mo *
                      %msup
                        %mi a
                        %mo *
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi z
                        %mo *
                      %msup
                        %mi a
                        %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %mi z
                      %mi a
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℏ
                      %mi z
                      %msup
                        %mi z
                        %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  e^{z a}
                  e^{z^\ast a^\ast}
                  \\;=\;
                  e^{z^\ast a^\ast}
                  e^{z a}
                  e^{\hbar z z^\ast}
          %p
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi z
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi z
                      %mo *
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z,z^\ast \in \mathbb{C}
          %h2#in_the_wick_algebra_of_free_quantum_fields In the Wick algebra of free quantum fields
          #MoyalStarProductOnMicrocausal.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hadamard+distribution"}> Hadamard
                \-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moyal+star+product"} Moyal star product
                on
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/microcausal+observables"} microcausal observables
                –
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abstract+Wick+algebra"} abstract Wick algebra
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E,\mathbf{L})
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field+theory"} free
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theory"} Lagrangian field theory
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green+hyperbolic+differential+equation"} Green hyperbolic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mi Φ
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \Phi = 0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+propagator"} causal propagator
              and let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi H
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mi i
                        %mn 2
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo +
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Delta_H
                    \\;=\;
                    \\tfrac{i}{2}\Delta + H
            %p
              be a corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wightman+propagator"} Wightman propagator
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hadamard+2-point+function"}> Hadamard 2-point function
              ).
            %p
              Then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star+product"} star product
              induced by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_H
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo ⋆
                      %mi H
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi prod
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi exp
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mo ∫
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi X
                            %mn 2
                      %mi ℏ
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi H
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mfrac
                        %mi δ
                        %mrow
                          %mi δ
                          %msup
                            %mi Φ
                            %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi x
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mfrac
                        %mi δ
                        %mrow
                          %mi δ
                          %msup
                            %mi Φ
                            %mi b
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi x
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mi dvol
                        %mi g
                      %mo )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A \star_H A
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    prod
                    \\circ
                    \\exp\left(
                    \\int_{X^2} \hbar \Delta_H^{a b}(x_1, x_2) \frac{\delta}{\delta \Phi^a(x_1)}
                    \\otimes \frac{\delta}{\delta \Phi^b(x_2)} dvol_g
                    \\right)
                    (P_1 \otimes P_2)
            %p
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/off-shell"} off-shell
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/microcausal+observables"} microcausal observables
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi ℱ
                      %mi mc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_1, A_2 \in \mathcal{F}_{mc}
              is well defined in that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+front+sets"} wave front sets
              involved in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products+of+distributions"} products of distributions
              that appear in expanding out the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential"} exponential
              satisfy
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H%C3%B6rmander%27s+criterion"} Hörmander's criterion
            %p
              Hence by the general properties of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star+products"} star products
              (
              %a{:href => "star+product#AssociativeAndUnitalStarProduct"}> this prop.
              ) this yields a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unital+algebra"} unital
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
              on the space of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+power+series"} formal power series
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℏ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hbar
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/off-shell"} off-shell
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/microcausal+observables"} microcausal observables
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi PolyObs
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi mc
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi ℏ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mo ⋆
                        %mi H
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left(
                    PolyObs(E)_{mc}[ [\hbar] ] \,,\, \star_H
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/off-shell"} off-shell
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wick+algebra"} Wick algebra
              corresponding to the choice of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wightman+propagator"} Wightman propagator
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            %p
              Moreover the image of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is an ideal with respect to this algebra structure, so that it descends to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/on-shell"} on-shell
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/microcausal+observables"} microcausal observables
              to yield the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/on-shell"} on-shell
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wick+algebra"} Wick algebra
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi PolyObs
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo ,
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi mc
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi ℏ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mo ⋆
                        %mi H
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left(
                    PolyObs(E,\mathbf{L})_{mc}[ [ \hbar ] ] \,,\, \star_H
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Finally, under
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+conjugation"} complex conjugation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^\ast
              these are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star+algebras"} star algebras
              in that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mn 1
                        %msub
                          %mo ⋆
                          %mi H
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mn 2
                        %mo )
                      %mo *
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mi A
                      %mn 2
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mo ⋆
                      %mi H
                    %msubsup
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                      %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left(
                    A_1 \star_H A_2
                    \\right)^\ast
                    \=
                    A_2^\ast \star_H A_1^\ast
                    \\,.
          %p
            For
            %strong proof
            see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wick+algebra"} Wick algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "Wick+algebra#MoyalStarProductOnMicrocausal"} this prop.
          #WickAlgebraIsFormalDeformationQuantization.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wick+algebra"} Wick algebra
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+deformation+quantization"} formal deformation quantization
                of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson-Peierls+bracket"} Poisson-Peierls algebra of observables
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E,\mathbf{L})
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field+theory"} free
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theory"} Lagrangian field theory
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green+hyperbolic+differential+equation"} Green hyperbolic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mi Φ
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \Phi = 0
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+propagator"} causal propagator
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi H
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mi i
                        %mn 2
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo +
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_H \;=\; \tfrac{i}{2}\Delta + H
              be a corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wightman+propagator"} Wightman propagator
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hadamard+2-point+function"}> Hadamard 2-point function
              ).
            %p
              Then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wick+algebra"} Wick algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi PolyObs
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo ,
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi mc
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi ℏ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mo ⋆
                        %mi H
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left( PolyObs(E,\mathbf{L})_{mc}[ [\hbar] ] \,,\, \star_H \right)
              from prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MoyalStarProductOnMicrocausal"}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+deformation+quantization"} formal deformation quantization
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+algebra"} Poisson algebra
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+phase+space"} covariant phase space
              given by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/on-shell"} on-shell
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial+observables"} polynomial observables
              equipped with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson-Peierls+bracket"} Poisson-Peierls bracket
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi PolyObs
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi mc
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi PolyObs
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi mc
                    %mo →
                    %mi PolyObs
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi mc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{-,-\} \;\colon\; PolyObs(E,\mathbf{L})_{mc} \otimes PolyObs(E,\mathbf{L})_{mc}  \to PolyObs(E,\mathbf{L})_{mc}
              in that for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi PolyObs
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi mc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_1, A_2 \in PolyObs(E,\mathbf{L})_{mc}
              we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo ⋆
                      %mi H
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi mod
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi ℏ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A_1 \star_H A_2
                    \\;=\;
                    A_1 \cdot A_2
                    \\;mod\;
                    \\hbar
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo ⋆
                      %mi H
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 2
                    %mo −
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mo ⋆
                      %mi H
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi i
                    %mi ℏ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi mod
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi ℏ
                      %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A_1 \star_H A_2
                    \-
                    A_2 \star_H A_1
                    \\;=\;
                    i \hbar \{A_1, A_2\}
                    \\;mod\;
                    \\hbar^2
                    \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Dito90"}> Dito 90
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "Wick+algebra#DutschFredenhagen01"} Dütsch-Fredenhagen 01
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MoyalStarProductOnMicrocausal"}
              this is immediate from the general properties of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star+product"} star product
              (
              %a{:href => "A+first+idea+of+quantum+field+theory+--+Quantization#MoyalStarProductIsFormalDeformationQuantization"}> this example
              ).
            %p
              Explicitly, consider, without restriction of generality,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mo ∫
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Φ
                      %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi dvol
                      %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_1 = \int (\alpha_1)_a(x) \mathbf{\Phi}^a(x)\, dvol_\Sigma(x)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mo ∫
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Φ
                      %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi dvol
                      %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_2 = \int (\alpha_2)_a(x) \mathbf{\Phi}^a(x)\, dvol_\Sigma(x)
              be two linear observables. Then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
